,"edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T23:29:30-07:00","id":1373848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1369038-anyone-else-really-eager-for-distant-worlds?p=1372564#post1372564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love a book of distant worlds at different times in the history of the Aeonverse. Picture a world first reached by Novas in the high tide of their first popularity. Then describing that world when rediscovered by Upeo wa Macho. Then touch upon chosen future periods. <br /> <br /> I could see a Mongo-like world ( complete with merciless tyrant and their beautiful child to fall in love with the right heroic PC) for Adventure! campaigns. And not rediscovered until the far future setting's time period. <br /> <br /> But a book of worlds in multiple time periods would be grand.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds like every other episode of Stargate, Which by the way is one of my favorite shows. Just spin the wheel I mean dial up the gate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T05:09:50-07:00","id":1373892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1369038-anyone-else-really-eager-for-distant-worlds?p=1373462#post1373462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going to draw from Marvel, I would recommend the UNS Elsa Bloodstone, or Abigail Brand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, if not the <i>UNS Elsa Bloodstone</i>, perhaps the <i>UNS Auntie Monica</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"